      "message": "It\u0027s frustrating we can\u0027t use C++20 and make SkRefCntBase constexpr by making the constructor and destructor `constexpr` (though then the destructor must always be empty and not have the debug assert). If we did that then this could be a `static constexpr SkEmptyFontMgr;` and we could just ref it and return it. This is all possible because SkEmptyFontMgr is stateless (aside from needing to support the reference count).\n\nSince we\u0027re stuck with C++17 we can\u0027t make this `constexpr`, but this can all safely be\n\n```\n    static SkEmptyFontMgr singleton;\n    return sk_ref_sp(\u0026singleton);\n```\n\nWhich should initialize the singleton thread safely the first time this is called.",
